sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2019-boundary-06> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Given the deep evolutionary conservation of ion-channel and neurotransmitter mechanisms between developmental and behavioural processes, the cognitive capacities of advanced brains are likely on a continuum with, and evolved from, much simpler computational processes conserved at both the functional and molecular levels.";
    dc:type "historical-inference";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Brain cognition lies on a continuum with conserved pre-neural computation";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “The Computational Boundary of a \"Self\": Developmental Bioelectricity Drives Multicellularity and Scale-Free Cognition”, Frontiers in psychology (2019), doi:10.3389/fpsyg.2019.02688; section “Body Patterning and Cognition: A Common Origin”. Scope: Nervous systems and their pre-neural cellular precursors across the tree of life"
}
